The ring is hidden because nao has no context-window size for `openaiCompatible` models, and the component bails out rather than guessing.

Here's the chain. `chat-input.tsx` renders `<ContextWindowRing />`, which returns `null` as soon as the backend reports a null context window:

```71:73:apps/frontend/src/components/ui/chat-input-context-window-ring.tsx
	if (!hasAssistantMessage || contextUsage.data?.contextWindow == null) {
		return null;
	}
```

The backend fills that field by looking the model up in nao's built-in model table:

```50:54:apps/backend/src/utils/chat-context-usage.ts
function getContextWindow({ provider, modelId }: { provider: LlmProvider; modelId: string }): number | null {
	const models = KNOWN_MODELS[providerKind(provider)] ?? [];
	const contextWindow = models.find((m) => m.id === modelId)?.contextWindow;
	return contextWindow ?? null;
}
```

For a provider like `openaiCompatible/my-vllm`, `providerKind` strips the instance name down to `openaiCompatible`, whose metadata declares `models: []` (provider-meta.ts line 792) since the model list is whatever the admin's endpoint serves. The lookup therefore never matches and returns null, so the ring disappears. The same thing happens for any custom model id you add on a built-in provider, since custom models aren't in `KNOWN_MODELS` either.

Worth noting that the runtime path does not have this gap: `createProviderModel` falls back to 200k when the model isn't known, so compaction still triggers on a sensible threshold.

```252:252:apps/backend/src/agents/providers.ts
	const contextWindow = providerConfig.models.find((m) => m.id === modelId)?.contextWindow ?? 200_000;
```

So it's only the UI that has no fallback. Two ways to close it: mirror the 200k default in `getContextWindow` (cheap, but the ring would show a made-up denominator), or add a `contextWindow` field to `CustomModelMetadata` (`apps/backend/src/types/llm.ts`) and the custom-model dialog, which already collects per-model costs, so admins can declare the real window — and keep hiding the ring only when nothing is declared. Want me to implement one of these?

So `CustomModelMetadata` only includes id, displayName, and costPerM—there's no contextWindow field available, which means there's no way to specify the context window for openaiCompatible models.
